{"y":1998,"label":"1997–98","coach":"Jim Calhoun","conf":"Big East","confDiv":"Big East 6","confShort":"Big East","w":32,"l":5,"cw":15,"cl":3,"confFinish":"1st in Big East","finish":"elite8","seed":2,"region":"East","apPre":12,"apHigh":6,"apFinal":6,"srs":20.67,"sos":7.89,"ortg":109.6,"drtg":91.3,"pace":69.9,"ppg":76.6,"oppg":63.9,"story":{"headline":"Rip's Buzzer-Beater, Elite Eight Again","text":"Freshman point guard Khalid El-Amin joined Rip Hamilton, and UConn roared to 32–5, won its Big East division and captured the Big East tournament, beating Syracuse 69–64 in the final. Hamilton was Big East Player of the Year and a consensus second-team All-American; El-Amin was Big East Rookie of the Year and tournament MVP; Calhoun won Big East Coach of the Year again. In the NCAA tournament UConn dispatched Fairleigh Dickinson and Indiana, then produced an unforgettable Sweet Sixteen finish: down 74–73 to Washington, the Huskies got three shots in the final 15 seconds, and Hamilton rebounded a Jake Voskuhl miss, then his own, before hitting the winner at the horn, 75–74. North Carolina ended the run in the Elite Eight, 75–64.","moments":[{"date":"1998-03-07","title":"Big East tournament final: W vs Syracuse","text":"UConn beat Syracuse 69–64 in the Big East tournament final at Madison Square Garden, New York."},{"date":"1998-03-12","title":"NCAA First Round: W vs Fairleigh Dickinson","text":"UConn beat Fairleigh Dickinson 93–85 in the NCAA tournament first round at MCI Center, Washington, D.C."},{"date":"1998-03-14","title":"NCAA Second Round: W vs Indiana","text":"UConn beat Indiana 78–68 in the NCAA tournament second round at MCI Center, Washington, D.C."},{"date":"1998-03-19","title":"Rip rips Washington","text":"Richard Hamilton's buzzer-beater beats Washington 75–74 in the Sweet Sixteen."},{"date":"1998-03-21","title":"NCAA Elite Eight: L vs North Carolina","text":"UConn lost to North Carolina 64–75 in the NCAA tournament elite eight at Greensboro Coliseum Complex, Greensboro, North Carolina."}],"honors":["Big East 6 Division regular-season champions","Big East tournament champions","Richard Hamilton – Consensus second-team All-American","Richard Hamilton – Big East Player of the Year","Jim Calhoun – Big East Coach of the Year","Khalid El-Amin – Big East Rookie/Freshman of the Year","Khalid El-Amin – Big East Tournament MVP","Richard Hamilton – First-team All-Big East"],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1997%E2%80%9398_Connecticut_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Hamilton_(basketball)","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khalid_El-Amin"]},"roster":[{"pid":"richard-hamilton-1","name":"Richard Hamilton","num":"32","cls":"SO","pos":"G","ht":"6-6","wt":185,"home":"Coatesville, PA","photo":"assets/players/richard-hamilton-1.jpg?v=b516aeaf","photoWide":true,"pg":{"g":37,"gs":37,"mp":32.5,"pts":21.5,"trb":4.4,"ast":2.4,"stl":1.5,"blk":0.2,"tov":2.2,"fg_pct":0.44,"fg3_pct":0.404,"ft_pct":0.843,"orb":1.5,"pf":1.9},"tot":{"mp":1203,"fg":270,"fga":614,"fg3":99,"fg3a":245,"ft":156,"fta":185,"orb":57,"drb":106,"trb":163,"ast":87,"stl":54,"blk":8,"tov":83,"pf":71,"pts":795,"g":37},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.566,"efg_pct":0.52,"usg_pct":null,"ast_pct":null,"trb_pct":null,"stl_pct":null,"blk_pct":null,"ws":6.6,"ws_per_40":0.22,"bpm":null,"obpm":null,"dbpm":null}},{"pid":"khalid-el-amin-1","name":"Khalid El-Amin","num":"42","cls":"FR","pos":"G","ht":"5-10","wt":200,"home":"Minneapolis, MN","photo":"assets/players/khalid-el-amin-1.jpg?v=a2623702","photoWide":true,"pg":{"g":37,"gs":36,"mp":29.9,"pts":16.0,"trb":2.9,"ast":4.2,"stl":1.8,"blk":0.1,"tov":2.7,"fg_pct":0.424,"fg3_pct":0.365,"ft_pct":0.796,"orb":0.7,"pf":1.8},"tot":{"mp":1106,"fg":211,"fga":498,"fg3":81,"fg3a":222,"ft":90,"fta":113,"orb":25,"drb":83,"trb":108,"ast":156,"stl":68,"blk":5,"tov":100,"pf":68,"pts":593,"g":37},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.537,"efg_pct":0.505,"usg_pct":